# Findings — release profile, source 93e5eed2990931dc9efde3837d27f1f92028eb60

Identity / method
- No product source edits. All source pointers below refer to the profiled commit above, not a later moving main.
- CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_DEBUG=true; compiler reported optimized + debuginfo. Generated an external dSYM with dsymutil (exit 0).
- Release Mach-O, uniquely named profile bundle, dSYM and trace binary all match UUID EF8C14AB-EB84-3857-B4A2-4BBF30C84A0B. Trace loaded image path is target/r2b/ReleaseProfile.app/Contents/MacOS/bboxy450-term-r2b, load base 0x1049dc000. The earlier debug trace is excluded.
- Instruments Time Profiler, 1ms CPU samples, waiting threads excluded. The stack filter is Gpu::draw, which also encloses surface acquire/present; it is not a signpost for only the encode timer. The app logs the separate phase times. Attribution uses sampled stack names; inlining can put small costs in the residual category. 1503 total samples, 1101 main-thread samples. Gpu::draw has 934ms sampled CPU. Warm subset excludes samples before first Gpu::draw sample +250ms, removing cold first paint; 889ms / 889 samples remain. The prescribed --smoke --meter changes one row and meter text; 15-pane topology/icons stay fixed. A completely identical manually triggered frame was not separately recorded.

Warm GPU draw/encode path sampled CPU (categories classified once, percentages of 889ms)
- atlas upload: 776ms, 87.29%.
- icon upload call at chrome/mod.rs:436: 723ms, 81.33%.
- glyph-mask upload call at chrome/mod.rs:428: 53ms, 5.96%.
- _platform_memmove self: 756ms, 85.04% (790ms across all encode_ops including first paint).
- queue submit: 43ms, 4.84%.
- other encode: 42ms, 4.72%.
- material passes: 15ms, 1.69%.
- text rasterization/shaping: 7ms, 0.79%.
- buffer creation: 5ms, 0.56%.
- group composite: 1ms, 0.11%.
- No warm pipeline-creation samples at 1ms resolution; one sample across all Gpu::draw including first paint. Pipeline construction is cached at chrome/mod.rs:411-413. Absence of a sample is not proof of zero work.

Top copy stack / exact mechanism
_platform_memmove
  wgpu_core::device::queue::Queue::write_texture (registry wgpu-core-30.0.1/src/device/queue.rs:999)
  wgpu_core::Global::queue_write_texture (same file:1943)
  wgpu::Queue::write_texture (registry wgpu-30.0.1/src/api/queue.rs:260)
  bbt_render::chrome::upload (crates/bbt-render/src/chrome/mod.rs:647)
  ChromeRenderer::draw_flat_with_load (same file:436 icon / :428 mask)
  ChromeRenderer::draw_overlay (:73)
  bboxy450_term::gpu::encode_ops (crates/bboxy450-term/src/gpu.rs:268)

Atos against the matching dSYM resolved sampled caller addresses 0x104aa3ffb -> mod.rs:436 and 0x104aa3fd3 -> mod.rs:428. The large caller is verified as the icon atlas, not guessed from function names.
- crates/bbt-render/src/chrome/icons.rs:17-20 fixes the CPU icon atlas at 2048x2048 RGBA = 16 MiB. It is immutable after construction, yet each nonempty flat chrome pass calls upload at :436.
- chrome/mod.rs:625-646 creates a new GPU texture in upload; :647-666 writes the ENTIRE pixels slice. :428 does the same for the glyph atlas regardless of whether it changed. There is no dirty/generation check or persistent GPU atlas in ChromeRenderer.
- The hot queue.rs:999 is an actual staging-buffer copy: allocate StagingBuffer then staging_buffer.write(&data[offset..]). This explains the sampled memmove cost.
- Uniform/storage buffers at chrome/mod.rs:418/:423, sampler at :446 and bindings at :452 are also recreated per pass, but their observed warm cost is small beside uploads.
- Whole-line text keys are cached at chrome/mod.rs:341-350; only a miss calls rasterize_at at :345. This is not primarily a text-shaping, layout, shader compilation or offscreen-group problem in the warm trace.

Unprofiled release baseline (same binary, exit 0)
- 21 frames; 10.002s idle / 0 frames / update 20. CPU meter p50=49.641ms, p99=99.887ms including first paint.
- Excluding first paint: encode median 47.3465ms, min 32.611ms, max 62.662ms; layout median 1.7930ms; draw median 0.0955ms.
- Early warm encode values were 32.611-34.645ms (matching Oracle's roughly 33ms); later samples were higher. The run did not isolate the cause of this variation, so no causal claim is made. Profiled run CPU p50=49.615ms / p99=106.750ms; timings and sampled CPU are distinct measures.

Proposed fix (not implemented; Oracle sequences it with Nyx)
1. Store GPU icon texture/view and linear sampler on ChromeRenderer, created once per renderer/device. Upload immutable icon pixels once, then reuse in every pass/frame.
2. Store the GPU glyph atlas too. Track inserted dirty rectangles and an atlas-growth generation; upload only new rectangles, allocate/full-upload only on actual growth. An unchanged atlas must cause zero write_texture calls, including between material-separated passes in the SAME frame. Keep in-flight old textures alive through bind-group references when growing.
3. Re-profile before changing layout/fonts/materials. If further work is needed, reuse uniform/instance storage through a per-frame arena or distinct pass offsets. A single overwritten shared uniform/storage buffer would make earlier encoded passes see later data; don't introduce that bug for reuse.

Expected encode after atlas retention: estimate, NOT a measurement.
- Amdahl estimate from the quiet ~33ms baseline: 33*(1-0.872891) = 4.195ms residual, plus dirty-glyph bookkeeping/uploads. Expect about 4-6ms on that baseline.
- Applied to this run's 47.3465ms median: residual 6.018ms, so roughly 6-8ms under the same conditions.
- CPU sampling share is not a guarantee of wall-time reduction; queue/driver waits and the R5 total <=4ms CPU goal still need measurement after the fix. No claim that 120Hz is achieved.

